From 91ae915140d2fd1db10b039e3c2cf2d57096f3f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nocdem <nocdem@cpunk.io>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Nodus EVM: 256-bit (32-byte) address type

- address/address payable/contract values are full 256-bit words (ABI size 32, storage 32, no packing)
- address cleanup is the identity in legacy and Yul IR codegen; no 160-bit masks
- explicit conversions only via uint256/bytes32; uint160/bytes20 conversions are errors
- address literals: 64 hex digits, mixed case, EIP-55 rule over 64 digits; 40-digit literals are errors
- removed optimizer rule AND(ADDRESS|CALLER|ORIGIN|COINBASE, 2**160-1) -> opcode
- external function types may only live on the stack (ABI/storage/memory packing does not fit)
- library linking (20-byte link references) refused; library deploy-time address is PUSH32
- SMTChecker models addresses as uint256
- version build tag nodus.addr256
---
